    {
      "id": "6dmuuf7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.1 Classical Art Forms"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Kerala is famous for two major classical dance forms: Kathakali (dance-drama) and Mohiniyattam (dance of the enchantress).",
        "Kalaripayattu, originating in Kerala, is recognized as one of the oldest continuous martial art traditions in the world.",
        "Malayalam belongs to the Dravidian language family and has a rich literary tradition influenced by Manipravalam.",
        "Kerala boasts six Jnanpith Award laureates, starting with G. Sankara Kurup receiving the inaugural award in 1965."
      ],
      "id": "emuqr7z"
    },
