    {
      "id": "b4yhr0u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.4 Literature and Languages"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k0j5a7u",
      "content": "Malayalam is the official language of Kerala and one of the classical languages of India. It was recognised as a classical language by the Government of India in 2013. Malayalam literature has a rich tradition spanning over 1,000 years."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "G. Sankara Kurup was the first recipient of the Jnanpith Award in 1965 for his Malayalam poetry collection 'Odakkuzhal'.",
        "Koodiyattam, a Sanskrit theatre form from Kerala, is officially recognized by UNESCO as a Masterpiece of Oral and Intangible Heritage.",
        "Thrissur Pooram, celebrated at Vadakkunnathan Temple, is commonly referred to as the 'Mother of all Poorams'."
      ],
      "id": "c3xtybf"
    },
